   "text": "I built the planetary set as four separate bodies, but it is not ready to print yet.\n\n- **Built:** a ring gear (70 mm outer diameter, 10 mm thick, 30 internal teeth), a sun (10 teeth) and three planets (10 teeth each, 120 degrees apart). The module is 2 mm with a 20 degree pressure angle, both my guesses.\n- **Not yet built:** the 0.3 mm print clearance from the sheet is not in the teeth, so the gears are at nominal size and may bind when printed. The teeth are straight-sided approximations, not true involutes.\n- **Plan error:** my plan listed the sun and planet root diameter as 17.5 mm. The correct value for this gear is 15 mm, so I built 15 mm.\n- **Check:** the plan check fails on feature count, 13 build steps against the 3 planned features. The bodies are closed and the thinnest wall is 2.15 mm, so this is a bookkeeping mismatch, not a geometry fault.\n- **Missing for print-in-place:** there is no carrier arm, so the planets have nothing holding them in place. Nothing has been arranged, sliced or sent to the printer.\n\nShould I add the 0.3 mm clearance and a carrier arm with planet pins before I arrange and slice?"
